        </?01M1C311TG98N6XJEKMCAZSJQ4>
      )>
      <Actor { role = "MissionObserver" project_ref = "host" } (
        <Description ?01M1C311TG98N6XJEKMCAZSJQ5>
        Observe BunFS/source bytes, VFS node identities and revisions, ordered overlay plans, strict mutation results, final Halfcode projections, authoring receipts, frozen Agent closures, compiled binaries and fresh recovery; coordinate overlapping resource work through current workspace evidence and .tmp/chat.jsonl.
        </?01M1C311TG98N6XJEKMCAZSJQ5>
      )>
      <Actor { role = "MissionReconciler" project_ref = "host" } (
        <Description ?01M1C311TG98N6XJEKMCAZSJQ6>
        Compare the actual topology with the invariant that consumers read one admitted Effective Eidolon VFS and Halfcode remains a one-way semantic projection; reject dual authorities, stale silent patches, random identities, registry-level overlay substitutions and unverifiable run drift.
        </?01M1C311TG98N6XJEKMCAZSJQ6>
      )>
      <Actor { role = "MissionApplier" project_ref = "host" } (
        <Description ?01M1C311TG98N6XJEKMCAZSJQ7>
        Create, execute, verify and archive bounded Tracks in their owner projects, use RED-to-GREEN and atomic readback evidence, preserve unrelated dirty work, and run final fresh gap-loop and independent verification without implementing product code directly in Mission files.
        </?01M1C311TG98N6XJEKMCAZSJQ7>
      )>
    ]>
  ]>
  <TaskSpace #space_establish-overlay-materialized-eidolon-vfs-and-halfcode-runtime { name = "establish-overlay-materialized-eidolon-vfs-and-halfcode-runtime" version = "1" child_mode = "dag" } (
    <SubNodes [
